  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q10-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Adrienne, Binh and Cooper were the only three competitors participating in a series of athletic events. In each event, the winner gets 3 points, second gets 2 points and third gets 1 point. After the events, Adrienne has 8 points, Binh has 11 points and Cooper has 5 points. In how many events did Adrienne come second? Perhaps you can do this without algebra?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Two events.\n\nBinh came second once and Cooper came second once; Adrienne came second in the other two events.",
      "worked": "Each event awards $3+2+1=6$ points. The total is $8+11+5=24$ points, so there were $24\\div6=4$ events.\n\nBinh's 11 points are one less than four wins, so Binh won three events and came second once. Cooper's 5 points are one more than four third places, so Cooper came third three times and second once.\n\nTheir second places occurred in different events. Adrienne therefore came second in the remaining $4-1-1=2$ events.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
